    quickAnswer: 'Under the MTP Act India 2021, women can terminate pregnancy up to 20 weeks with one doctor approval. No husband or family permission is needed. Up to 24 weeks is allowed for rape survivors, minors, and special cases. Abortion is a legal right in India.',
    procedure: "MTP & Abortion",
    keywords: ["mtp-act-india-2021-womens-rights", "MTP Act India 2021 — Your Complete Rights for Abortion"],
    body: "The Medical Termination of Pregnancy Act India 2021 is a landmark amendment that significantly expands women's rights to safe and legal abortion. Here is everything you need to know.\n\nKey Changes in MTP Act 2021\n\nThe 2021 amendment increased the upper gestational limit from 20 to 24 weeks for special categories. It removed the requirement of approval from two doctors for terminations between 12 and 20 weeks — now only one doctor's approval is needed. It also expanded the list of special categories who can terminate up to 24 weeks.\n\nWho Can Terminate Up to 24 Weeks?\n\nSurvivors of rape or sexual assault. Minors (under 18 years). Women with disabilities (physical or mental). Women with change in marital status during pregnancy (divorce or widowhood). Women with foetal abnormalities. Women in emergency situations.\n\n\\n\\nSpeaking to an expert is completely free and confidential. Call MySurgery at 8588967050 or WhatsApp us to connect with an experienced doctor in your city within 30 minutes.\\n\\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588967050\n\nDo I Need My Husband's Permission?\n\nNo. The MTP Act India 2021 is very clear — only the woman's own informed consent is required. Your husband, partner, parents, or in-laws have no legal right to prevent you from accessing abortion services. This is your legal right.\n\nExpert Doctor for This Procedure\\n\\nDr. Meenakshi Ahuja (MD (OBG), FICOG) — 30 years of experience — practices at Fortis La Femme, Delhi. Call MySurgery at 8588967050 to book a consultation with Dr. Meenakshi Ahuja or a similar expert in your city.\n\nConfidentiality Under the MTP Act\n\nThe law requires complete confidentiality. Doctors and hospitals are legally prohibited from disclosing your identity or medical details to anyone without your consent. MySurgery's systems comply with the highest confidentiality standards.\n\n\\n\\nSpeaking to an expert is completely free and confidential. Call MySurgery at 8588967050 or WhatsApp us to connect with an experienced doctor in your city within 30 minutes.\\n\\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588967050\n\nWhere to Access Safe Abortion in India\n\nAbortion must be performed by a registered medical practitioner (RMP) at an approved place — a government hospital or a private facility registered under the MTP Act. MySurgery only works with registered, approved facilities across all cities.\n\nWhat If You Are Refused?\n\nUnder the MTP Act, refusing a legal abortion request without medical grounds is a violation of your rights. If you face refusal or judgment, call MySurgery immediately at 8588967050 and we will connect you with a registered gynaecologist who will help you.\n\n\\n\\nSpeaking to an expert is completely free and confidential. Call MySurgery at 8588967050 or WhatsApp us to connect with an experienced doctor in your city within 30 minutes.\\n\\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588967050",
