    readTime: "8 min read",
    quickAnswer: 'Survivors of rape or sexual assault can terminate pregnancy up to 24 weeks in India under the MTP Act 2021. No police report is required for MTP. No husband or family permission is needed. The procedure is completely confidential and free at government hospitals.',
