    slug: "mtp-second-trimester-india-12-20-weeks",
    title: "Second Trimester Abortion in India (12 to 20 Weeks) — Complete Guide",
    excerpt: "Second Trimester Abortion in India (12 to 20 Weeks) — Complete Guide — Expert guide with costs, legal information, doctor insights, and free consultation.",
    date: "2026-04-01",
    author: "Dr. Rekha Wadhwani",
    authorTitle: "MS (OBG), 19 years experience, Medanta Gurugram",
    category: "Gynecology",
    readTime: "8 min read",
    quickAnswer: 'Second trimester abortion (12 to 20 weeks) is legal in India and costs Rs 12,000 to Rs 25,000. It requires medical preparation, is more complex than first trimester abortion, but is still safe at registered hospitals with experienced gynaecologists.',
    procedure: "MTP & Abortion",
    keywords: ["mtp-second-trimester-india-12-20-weeks", "Second Trimester Abortion in India (12 to 20 Weeks) — Comple"],
    body: 'Second trimester abortion (12 to 20 weeks) is less common than first trimester abortion but is sometimes necessary. Here is a complete guide.\n\nWhy Second Trimester Abortion?\n\nLate discovery of pregnancy due to irregular periods, hormonal conditions, or denial. Foetal abnormalities detected on 18 to 20 week anomaly scan. Change in life circumstances (relationship breakdown, job loss). Young women or teenagers who delay seeking help. Situations of domestic violence or sexual abuse. All these situations are legally covered under the MTP Act India 2021.\n\n\\n\\nSpeaking to an expert is completely free and confidential. Call MySurgery at 8588967050 or WhatsApp us to connect with an experienced doctor in your city within 30 minutes.\\n\\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588967050\n\nMethods for Second Trimester Abortion in India\n\n12 to 16 weeks: Dilation and Evacuation (D&E) — the preferred method. The cervix is prepared over 1 to 2 days with medication to soften and dilate it. Then the uterine contents are removed under anaesthesia. Takes 30 to 60 minutes. Hospital stay of 4 to 8 hours.\n\n16 to 20 weeks: Medical induction combined with surgical evacuation. Medicines cause the uterus to contract and expel the pregnancy. May take several hours and may require an overnight stay.\n\nCost: Rs 12,000 to Rs 25,000 depending on gestational age, hospital, and city.\n\nExpert Doctor for This Procedure\\n\\nDr. Rekha Wadhwani (MS (OBG)) — 19 years of experience — practices at Medanta, Gurugram. Call MySurgery at 8588967050 to book a consultation with Dr. Rekha Wadhwani or a similar expert in your city.\n\nIs Second Trimester Abortion Safe?\n\nYes, when performed by experienced gynaecologists at registered hospitals. Complication rates are higher than first trimester abortion but remain below 2% at quality centres. The key is choosing a doctor with experience in second trimester procedures.\n\n\\n\\nSpeaking to an expert is completely free and confidential. Call MySurgery at 8588967050 or WhatsApp us to connect with an experienced doctor in your city within 30 minutes.\\n\\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588967050\n\nSecond Trimester Abortion Requires Planning\n\nUnlike first trimester procedures which can often be done on the same day second trimester procedures require preparation and planning. Cervical ripening medications are usually given 1 to 2 days before the procedure. MySurgery helps you plan the entire process including accommodation near the hospital.\n\nDo Not Delay\n\nIf you are considering second trimester MTP please contact MySurgery immediately. Gestational age increases every day and earlier procedures are always simpler and safer. Call 8588967050 or WhatsApp us for priority assistance.\n\n\\n\\nSpeaking to an expert is completely free and confidential. Call MySurgery at 8588967050 or WhatsApp us to connect with an experienced doctor in your city within 30 minutes.\\n\\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588967050',
