    authorTitle: "MS (OBG), Fellowship Laparoscopic Gynaecology, 20 years experience, Medanta Lucknow Lucknow",
    category: "Gynecology",
    readTime: "8 min read",
    quickAnswer: 'Both MTP (abortion) and adoption are legal options for an unplanned pregnancy in India. MTP is available up to 20 weeks. Adoption allows the pregnancy to continue and the child to be placed with a family. Both are personal decisions with no right or wrong answer.',
    procedure: "MTP & Abortion",
    keywords: ["mtp-vs-adoption-india-making-the-decision", "MTP vs Adoption in India — Understanding Your Options"],
    body: "Facing an unplanned pregnancy can be one of the most difficult experiences in a woman's life. MySurgery believes in providing information about all legal options so you can make the best decision for yourself.\n\nOption 1 — MTP (Medical Termination of Pregnancy)\n\nMTP is a legal right for women in India up to 20 weeks of pregnancy. It is a safe and common procedure when performed by a registered doctor. It allows you to end the pregnancy without continuing to term. Physical recovery is typically quick (1 to 2 weeks). Emotional recovery varies from person to person. There is no right or wrong emotional response.\n\n\\n\\nSpeaking to an expert is completely free and confidential. Call MySurgery at 8588967050 or WhatsApp us to connect with an experienced doctor in your city within 30 minutes.\\n\\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588967050\n\nOption 2 — Continuing the Pregnancy and Parenting\n\nYou may choose to continue the pregnancy and raise the child yourself, with a partner, or with family support. MySurgery's gynaecology partners can provide antenatal care if you choose this path.\n\nOption 3 — Continuing the Pregnancy and Adoption\n\nIndia's Central Adoption Resource Authority (CARA) manages a regulated adoption system. If you continue the pregnancy and decide you are unable to raise the child you can place the child for adoption through CARA-registered agencies. This is a legal process with full support for birth mothers.\n\nExpert Doctor for This Procedure\\n\\nDr. Sunita Varma (MS (OBG), Fellowship Laparoscopic Gynaecology) — 20 years of experience — practices at Medanta Lucknow, Lucknow. Call MySurgery at 8588967050 to book a consultation with Dr. Sunita Varma or a similar expert in your city.\n\nSupport for Your Decision\n\nWhatever decision you make MySurgery's female care coordinators are here to listen without judgment. We provide information about all options and connect you with the right support — whether that is MTP services, antenatal care, counselling, or legal aid.\n\n\\n\\nSpeaking to an expert is completely free and confidential. Call MySurgery at 8588967050 or WhatsApp us to connect with an experienced doctor in your city within 30 minutes.\\n\\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588967050\n\nImportant: Time Matters for MTP\n\nIf you are considering MTP please do not delay in making your decision. The gestational age increases every day and earlier procedures are simpler, safer, and less expensive. If you decide on MTP after consulting all options call MySurgery immediately at 8588967050.\n\n\\n\\nSpeaking to an expert is completely free and confidential. Call MySurgery at 8588967050 or WhatsApp us to connect with an experienced doctor in your city within 30 minutes.\\n\\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588967050",
