    body: 'Phimosis — tight foreskin that cannot be retracted — affects an estimated 1 to 2% of adult men in India. Here is a complete guide to treatment options and costs.\n\nWhat Is Phimosis?\n\nPhimosis is a condition where the foreskin (prepuce) is too tight to be pulled back over the glans (head) of the penis. It can be congenital (present from birth) or acquired (developed over time due to scarring, infection, or lichen sclerosus). Symptoms include pain during erection, difficulty urinating, recurrent infections under the foreskin, and foreskin ballooning during urination.\n\nPhimosis Treatment Options\n\nSteroid cream — for mild phimosis, applied for 4 to 8 weeks, success rate 70 to 80%. Gentle stretching exercises — combined with steroid cream, works for mild cases. Preputioplasty — surgical widening of the foreskin opening while preserving the foreskin, suitable for mild to moderate phimosis. Laser or ZSR circumcision — complete removal of the foreskin, permanent cure, suitable for all grades including severe BXO.\n\n\\n\\nSpeaking to an expert is completely free and confidential. Call MySurgery at 8588967050 or WhatsApp us to connect with an experienced doctor in your city within 30 minutes.\\n\\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588967050\n\nPhimosis Treatment Cost in India 2026\n\nSteroid cream course: Rs 500 to Rs 1,500 (treatment plus doctor fees). Preputioplasty: Rs 15,000 to Rs 35,000. Laser circumcision: Rs 15,000 to Rs 45,000. ZSR circumcision: Rs 12,000 to Rs 42,000.\n\nExpert Doctor for This Procedure\\n\\nDr. Sandeep Nunia (MCh (Urology)) — 20 years of experience — practices at Max Hospital, Delhi. Call MySurgery at 8588967050 to book a consultation with Dr. Sandeep Nunia or a similar expert in your city.\n\nWhich Treatment Is Best for Phimosis?\n\nMild phimosis (foreskin partially retractable): try steroid cream for 8 weeks first. Moderate phimosis (foreskin cannot retract at all): preputioplasty or circumcision depending on preference. Severe phimosis with BXO (scarring): circumcision is the only effective treatment. Phimosis with recurrent infections: circumcision is strongly recommended.\n\n\\n\\nSpeaking to an expert is completely free and confidential. Call MySurgery at 8588967050 or WhatsApp us to connect with an experienced doctor in your city within 30 minutes.\\n\\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588967050\n\nRecovery After Phimosis Treatment\n\nLaser or ZSR circumcision for phimosis: same-day discharge, return to work in 2 to 3 days, sexual activity after 4 to 6 weeks, permanent resolution of phimosis.\n\nCall MySurgery at 8588967050 for a confidential consultation with a urologist who will examine you and recommend the best treatment for your specific situation.\n\n\\n\\nSpeaking to an expert is completely free and confidential. Call MySurgery at 8588967050 or WhatsApp us to connect with an experienced doctor in your city within 30 minutes.\\n\\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588967050',
