    quickAnswer: 'Recurrent balanitis (infection of the glans penis) that does not respond to antifungals and antibiotics is best treated with circumcision. Laser or ZSR circumcision permanently eliminates the moist environment where bacteria and fungi thrive.',
    procedure: "Circumcision (Laser/ZSR)",
    keywords: ["circumcision-balanitis-recurrent-infection", "Circumcision for Recurrent Balanitis — When Surgery Is the A"],
    body: 'Recurrent balanitis is one of the most frustrating urological conditions — recurring episodes of inflammation and infection of the glans penis that keep coming back despite treatment. Circumcision provides a permanent solution.\n\nWhat Is Balanitis?\n\nBalanitis is inflammation and infection of the glans (head) of the penis and sometimes the foreskin (posthitis). It causes redness, swelling, discharge, itching, and pain. It is caused by bacteria, fungi (especially Candida), or both. Poor hygiene, tight foreskin (phimosis), diabetes, and immunosuppression are common risk factors.\n\nWhy Does Balanitis Keep Coming Back?\n\nIn men with a foreskin the warm, moist environment under the foreskin provides ideal conditions for bacteria and fungi to grow. Even after successful treatment with antifungals and antibiotics the same conditions exist and infection recurs. This pattern of recurrent balanitis is a clear indication for circumcision.\n\n\\n\\nSpeaking to an expert is completely free and confidential. Call MySurgery at 8588967050 or WhatsApp us to connect with an experienced doctor in your city within 30 minutes.\\n\\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588967050\n\nHow Circumcision Cures Recurrent Balanitis\n\nCircumcision removes the foreskin which eliminates the enclosed moist environment where pathogens multiply. After circumcision the glans is exposed to air and is easier to keep clean. The vast majority of men with recurrent balanitis who undergo circumcision have complete resolution of the problem.\n\nExpert Doctor for This Procedure\\n\\nDr. Sandeep Nunia (MCh (Urology)) — 20 years of experience — practices at Max Hospital, Delhi. Call MySurgery at 8588967050 to book a consultation with Dr. Sandeep Nunia or a similar expert in your city.\n\nCost of Circumcision for Balanitis in India\n\nLaser circumcision: Rs 15,000 to Rs 45,000. ZSR circumcision: Rs 12,000 to Rs 42,000. Conventional: Rs 10,000 to Rs 25,000. Circumcision for recurrent balanitis may be covered by health insurance — MySurgery helps check your policy.\n\n\\n\\nSpeaking to an expert is completely free and confidential. Call MySurgery at 8588967050 or WhatsApp us to connect with an experienced doctor in your city within 30 minutes.\\n\\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588967050\n\nIs Circumcision Covered for Balanitis?\n\nYes, circumcision performed for medical reasons including recurrent balanitis, phimosis, and BXO is typically covered by health insurance in India. MySurgery helps with insurance pre-authorisation and cashless claims at partner hospitals.\n\nIf you have recurrent balanitis call MySurgery at 8588967050 for a confidential consultation with a urologist.\n\n\\n\\nSpeaking to an expert is completely free and confidential. Call MySurgery at 8588967050 or WhatsApp us to connect with an experienced doctor in your city within 30 minutes.\\n\\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588967050',
