    category: "Urology",
    readTime: "8 min read",
    quickAnswer: 'Infant circumcision costs Rs 8,000 to Rs 20,000 in India. For children under 5 general anaesthesia is used. For children over 5 local anaesthesia is preferred. ZSR technique is commonly used for child circumcision. Healing is faster in younger children.',
    procedure: "Circumcision (Laser/ZSR)",
    keywords: ["circumcision-child-infant-india-guide", "Infant and Child Circumcision in India — Safety, Age, and Co"],
    body: 'Circumcision in infants and children is a common procedure in India performed for religious reasons in Muslim families and for medical indications. Here is a complete guide.\n\nAge for Infant Circumcision in India\n\nIn the Muslim community infant circumcision (khitan) is typically performed between 7 days and 40 days of birth (traditional) or any time during childhood. Medically it is often recommended between 6 months and 1 year when the baby is healthy but still young enough for fast healing.\n\nCircumcision in Children Under 5\n\nFor infants and young children general anaesthesia (brief, very safe at modern hospitals) is used so the child feels no pain during the procedure. ZSR circumcision is commonly used in this age group for its speed and precision. The procedure takes 10 to 15 minutes and the child typically wakes up quickly. Healing in young children is remarkably fast — 5 to 7 days.\n\n\\n\\nSpeaking to an expert is completely free and confidential. Call MySurgery at 8588967050 or WhatsApp us to connect with an experienced doctor in your city within 30 minutes.\\n\\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588967050\n\nCircumcision Cost for Infants and Children in India\n\nInfant/child circumcision (general anaesthesia): Rs 12,000 to Rs 30,000 depending on city and hospital. The higher cost compared to adult circumcision under local anaesthesia reflects the anaesthesia costs. Delhi and Mumbai: Rs 15,000 to Rs 30,000. Tier-2 cities: Rs 10,000 to Rs 20,000.\n\nExpert Doctor for This Procedure\\n\\nDr. Amit Khanna (MCh (Urology), Fellowship Andrology) — 14 years of experience — practices at Jaypee Hospital, Noida. Call MySurgery at 8588967050 to book a consultation with Dr. Amit Khanna or a similar expert in your city.\n\nIs Circumcision Safe for Infants?\n\nYes. Infant and child circumcision performed by a qualified paediatric surgeon or urologist at a registered hospital is safe. The complication rate is below 1%. It is important to choose a doctor experienced in paediatric circumcision. Never use traditional non-medical circumcision for infants — the risk of serious complications is high.\n\n\\n\\nSpeaking to an expert is completely free and confidential. Call MySurgery at 8588967050 or WhatsApp us to connect with an experienced doctor in your city within 30 minutes.\\n\\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588967050\n\nPost-Procedure Care for Infant Circumcision\n\nKeep the area clean with gentle washing. Apply prescribed antibiotic ointment. Change nappies frequently. Monitor for signs of infection (redness, swelling, fever). The wound heals in 5 to 10 days in infants.\n\nFor child circumcision older children may find the initial soreness distressing. Explain to the child that the discomfort will pass and reassure them regularly. Pain medication as prescribed makes the recovery comfortable.\n\n\\n\\nSpeaking to an expert is completely free and confidential. Call MySurgery at 8588967050 or WhatsApp us to connect with an experienced doctor in your city within 30 minutes.\\n\\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588967050',
