    slug: "laparoscopic-vs-open-hernia-surgery-india",
    title: "Laparoscopic vs Open Hernia Surgery in India — Which Is Better?",
    excerpt: "Laparoscopic vs Open Hernia Surgery in India — Which Is Better? — Expert guide with costs, doctor insights, and free consultation.",
    date: "2026-04-29",
    author: "Dr. Nitin Jha",
    authorTitle: "MS General Surgery, FMAS, FIAGES, 19 years experience, Fortis Hospital Noida Noida",
    category: "Laparoscopy",
    readTime: "7 min read",
    quickAnswer: "Laparoscopic hernia surgery is better for most patients \u2014 smaller cuts, less pain, faster recovery (5-7 days vs 4-6 weeks), and lower recurrence rates. Open surgery may be preferred for very large hernias, strangulated hernias, or when laparoscopic is not available.",
    procedure: "Hernia Surgery",
    keywords: ["laparoscopic-vs-open-hernia-surgery-india", "Laparoscopic vs Open Hernia Surgery in India — Which Is Bett"],
    body: "Laparoscopic vs Open Hernia Surgery \u2014 The Complete Comparison\n\nThe most common question hernia patients ask is whether they should have laparoscopic (keyhole) or open surgery. Here is an evidence-based comparison.\n\nWhat Is Laparoscopic Hernia Repair?\n\nLaparoscopic hernia repair is performed through 3 small incisions (5mm to 10mm each). A tiny camera (laparoscope) is inserted and the surgeon repairs the hernia using instruments inserted through the other incisions. A mesh is placed to strengthen the abdominal wall. The patient goes home the same day or after one night.\n\nWhat Is Open Hernia Surgery?\n\nOpen hernia repair involves a single larger incision (5 to 10cm) directly over the hernia. The hernia sac is reduced and a mesh is placed to repair the defect. The incision is closed with sutures. Recovery takes 4 to 6 weeks.\n\n\n\nCall MySurgery at 8588967050 or WhatsApp us for a free consultation with an experienced hernia surgeon in your city. Callback within 30 minutes.\n\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588967050\n\nComparison Table\n\nPain after surgery: Laparoscopic \u2014 mild, controlled with oral painkillers. Open \u2014 moderate to severe for first week.\n\nIncision size: Laparoscopic \u2014 3 cuts of 5 to 10mm. Open \u2014 1 cut of 5 to 10cm.\n\nHospital stay: Laparoscopic \u2014 same day or 1 night. Open \u2014 1 to 3 nights.\n\nReturn to desk work: Laparoscopic \u2014 5 to 7 days. Open \u2014 2 to 3 weeks.\n\nReturn to physical work: Laparoscopic \u2014 2 to 3 weeks. Open \u2014 4 to 6 weeks.\n\nRecurrence rate: Laparoscopic \u2014 1 to 2%. Open \u2014 2 to 5%.\n\nCost: Laparoscopic \u2014 Rs 55,000 to Rs 1,40,000. Open \u2014 Rs 35,000 to Rs 80,000.\n\n\n\nExpert Surgeon Featured\n\nDr. Nitin Jha (MS General Surgery, FMAS, FIAGES) \u2014 19 years of experience \u2014 practices at Fortis Hospital Noida, Noida. Call MySurgery at 8588967050 to book a consultation.\n\nWhen Is Open Surgery Better?\n\nVery large hernias with significant tissue loss. Strangulated or obstructed hernia requiring emergency surgery. Previous multiple abdominal surgeries making laparoscopic difficult. Patients who cannot tolerate general anaesthesia (open can be done under spinal).\n\nWhen Is Laparoscopic Surgery Better?\n\nFor most inguinal, umbilical, and small incisional hernias. Bilateral inguinal hernias \u2014 both sides repaired in one surgery. Recurrent hernias after previous open repair. Patients who need quick return to work or physical activity.\n\n\n\nCall MySurgery at 8588967050 or WhatsApp us for a free consultation with an experienced hernia surgeon in your city. Callback within 30 minutes.\n\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588967050\n\nWhich Technique Has Lower Recurrence?\n\nMultiple studies show laparoscopic hernia repair has a recurrence rate of 1 to 2% compared to 2 to 5% for open surgery. The recurrence difference is most pronounced for inguinal hernias where laparoscopic (TEP or TAPP) repair is now considered the gold standard at experienced centres.\n\nMySurgery only partners with surgeons experienced in laparoscopic hernia repair. Call 8588967050 for a free consultation.\n\n\n\nCall MySurgery at 8588967050 or WhatsApp us for a free consultation with an experienced hernia surgeon in your city. Callback within 30 minutes.\n\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588967050",
