    keywords: ["inguinal-hernia-surgery-cost-india-2026", "Inguinal Hernia Surgery Cost in India 2026 — Complete Guide"],
    body: "Inguinal Hernia Surgery in India \u2014 Complete Cost and Treatment Guide\n\nInguinal hernia is the most common type of hernia, accounting for 75% of all hernia cases. It is more common in men. Here is everything you need to know about inguinal hernia surgery in India.\n\nWhat Is Inguinal Hernia?\n\nAn inguinal hernia occurs when tissue, usually part of the intestine, pushes through a weak spot in the abdominal muscles in the groin area. The bulge can be painful and becomes more noticeable when you cough, bend over, or lift something heavy.\n\nSymptoms of Inguinal Hernia\n\nA bulge in the groin area that may disappear when lying down. Pain or discomfort in the groin especially when bending, coughing, or lifting. Feeling of heaviness or dragging sensation in the groin. Weakness or pressure in the groin. Occasionally nausea and vomiting if intestine gets trapped.\n\n\n\nCall MySurgery at 8588967050 or WhatsApp us for a free consultation with an experienced hernia surgeon in your city. Callback within 30 minutes.\n\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588967050\n\nTypes of Inguinal Hernia Repair in India\n\nTEP (Totally Extraperitoneal): The most popular laparoscopic technique. Mesh is placed without entering the peritoneal cavity. Fastest recovery. Cost: Rs 60,000 to Rs 1,20,000.\n\nTAPP (Transabdominal Preperitoneal): Laparoscopic repair entering the peritoneum. Allows better visualisation. Cost: Rs 55,000 to Rs 1,10,000.\n\nLichtenstein Repair (Open): The gold standard open technique. Tension-free mesh repair. Cost: Rs 35,000 to Rs 70,000.\n\n\n\nExpert Surgeon Featured\n\nDr. Rakesh Kumar (MS General Surgery, Fellowship Minimal Access Surgery) \u2014 22 years of experience \u2014 practices at Fortis Hospital Gurugram, Gurugram. Call MySurgery at 8588967050 to book a consultation.\n\nInguinal Hernia Surgery Cost by City\n\nDelhi: Rs 55,000 to Rs 1,10,000. Gurugram: Rs 60,000 to Rs 1,20,000. Mumbai: Rs 65,000 to Rs 1,30,000. Bangalore: Rs 55,000 to Rs 1,10,000. Chennai: Rs 50,000 to Rs 1,00,000. Kochi: Rs 45,000 to Rs 90,000. Tier-2 cities: Rs 35,000 to Rs 70,000.\n\n\n\nCall MySurgery at 8588967050 or WhatsApp us for a free consultation with an experienced hernia surgeon in your city. Callback within 30 minutes.\n\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588967050\n\nBilateral Inguinal Hernia \u2014 Both Sides in One Surgery\n\nIf you have hernias on both sides, laparoscopic repair is strongly preferred because both sides can be repaired through the same 3 small incisions in a single surgery. Cost for bilateral inguinal hernia repair: Rs 75,000 to Rs 1,60,000.\n\nIs Inguinal Hernia Surgery Urgent?\n\nNot always \u2014 but do not delay unnecessarily. A hernia will not heal on its own and typically grows larger over time. The risk of dangerous complications (strangulation, obstruction) increases with time. If the hernia is painful, enlarging, or cannot be pushed back, consult a surgeon urgently.\n\n\n\nCall MySurgery at 8588967050 or WhatsApp us for a free consultation with an experienced hernia surgeon in your city. Callback within 30 minutes.\n\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588967050",
