    body: "Hernia Surgery Recovery \u2014 Complete Day by Day Guide\n\nUnderstanding what to expect after hernia surgery reduces anxiety and helps you recover faster. Here is a detailed recovery guide for both laparoscopic and open hernia repair.\n\nDay of Surgery\n\nYou will be in the recovery room for 1 to 2 hours after the procedure. Mild nausea from anaesthesia is common and passes quickly. You will have 3 small dressings (laparoscopic) or one larger dressing (open). You can eat light food once fully awake. Most patients go home the same evening or after one night.\n\nDay 1 to 3 After Surgery\n\nMild to moderate pain and discomfort at the incision sites and in the groin or abdomen. Take prescribed painkillers regularly even if pain is mild \u2014 this prevents pain from building up. Walk slowly around the house from day 1. Avoid lifting anything heavier than a cup of tea. Eat soft, easily digestible foods. Keep the dressings dry. Mild swelling and bruising around the incision sites is completely normal.\n\n\n\nCall MySurgery at 8588967050 or WhatsApp us for a free consultation with an experienced hernia surgeon in your city. Callback within 30 minutes.\n\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588967050\n\nDay 4 to 7 After Surgery\n\nPain significantly reduces. Swelling begins to decrease. You can shower carefully (avoid soaking the wound). Return to desk work is possible for most patients at day 5 to 7. Light walking and slow stairs are fine. Continue to avoid lifting, straining, and heavy exertion.\n\n\n\nExpert Surgeon Featured\n\nDr. Faisal Mumtaz (MS General Surgery, Member ASI) \u2014 23 years of experience \u2014 practices at Apollo Hospitals Delhi, Delhi. Call MySurgery at 8588967050 to book a consultation.\n\nWeek 2 to 3 After Surgery\n\nMost patients feel close to normal by week 2. Light household activities are fine. Short drives are possible by day 7 to 10. Avoid gym, sports, and heavy lifting until week 3 to 4. Follow-up appointment at 2 weeks with your surgeon.\n\nWeek 4 to 6 After Surgery\n\nFull recovery for most patients. Laparoscopic hernia repair: cleared for all activities including gym and heavy lifting at 4 to 6 weeks. Open hernia repair: cleared for heavy work at 6 to 8 weeks. The mesh is fully integrated by 6 weeks.\n\n\n\nCall MySurgery at 8588967050 or WhatsApp us for a free consultation with an experienced hernia surgeon in your city. Callback within 30 minutes.\n\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588967050\n\nFoods to Eat and Avoid After Hernia Surgery\n\nEat: high-fibre foods (fruits, vegetables, whole grains), plenty of water, light proteins (dal, eggs, fish). Avoid: spicy food for first week, foods that cause gas (cabbage, beans, carbonated drinks), alcohol for 2 weeks, heavy meals.\n\nWarning Signs \u2014 Call Your Surgeon If\n\nFever above 38 degrees. Increasing redness, warmth, or discharge from the wound. Severe or worsening pain after day 3. Inability to urinate. Vomiting or inability to eat.\n\n\n\nCall MySurgery at 8588967050 or WhatsApp us for a free consultation with an experienced hernia surgeon in your city. Callback within 30 minutes.\n\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588967050",
