    body: "Sports Hernia in India \u2014 Complete Guide\n\nSports hernia is increasingly recognised in Indian athletes, particularly those involved in football, cricket, hockey, and running. Here is everything you need to know.\n\nWhat Is Sports Hernia?\n\nSports hernia (also called athletic pubalgia) is not a true hernia in the conventional sense. There is no visible bulge. It is a tear or weakening of the muscles and tendons in the lower abdomen and groin area. It causes chronic groin pain that is made worse by sports activities.\n\nWho Gets Sports Hernia?\n\nSports hernia is most common in football players, hockey players, cricketers, tennis players, and long-distance runners. It is more common in men. The repetitive twisting and turning movements in these sports put excessive stress on the groin muscles.\n\n\n\nCall MySurgery at 8588967050 or WhatsApp us for a free consultation with an experienced hernia surgeon in your city. Callback within 30 minutes.\n\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588967050\n\nSymptoms of Sports Hernia\n\nChronic groin pain that comes on gradually. Pain that worsens with specific activities (kicking, twisting, sprinting). Pain that may radiate to the inner thigh or lower abdomen. Tenderness when pressing on the pubic bone area. Pain that eases with rest but returns with sport. No visible bulge (unlike a true inguinal hernia).\n\nDiagnosis of Sports Hernia in India\n\nSports hernia is diagnosed by clinical examination combined with MRI of the pelvis and groin. The MRI shows tears in the adductor muscles, rectus abdominis, or conjoint tendon. A hernia specialist or sports medicine physician should evaluate the condition.\n\n\n\nExpert Surgeon Featured\n\nDr. Arun Prasad (MS General Surgery, FMAS, FIAGES) \u2014 35 years of experience \u2014 practices at Apollo Hospitals Delhi, Delhi. Call MySurgery at 8588967050 to book a consultation.\n\nTreatment of Sports Hernia in India\n\nConservative treatment (first line): rest from sport for 6 to 12 weeks, physiotherapy focusing on core strengthening, anti-inflammatory medicines, and local steroid injection. Success rate 50 to 70%.\n\nSurgical treatment (for failed conservative): laparoscopic repair of the torn muscles and tendons. The surgeon reinforces the posterior inguinal wall and repairs any associated true hernia. Cost in India: Rs 60,000 to Rs 1,20,000.\n\n\n\nCall MySurgery at 8588967050 or WhatsApp us for a free consultation with an experienced hernia surgeon in your city. Callback within 30 minutes.\n\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588967050\n\nRecovery After Sports Hernia Surgery\n\nReturn to light jogging: 4 to 6 weeks. Return to full training: 3 to 4 months. Return to competitive sport: 4 to 6 months.\n\nPhysiotherapy is essential both before and after surgery for optimal results. MySurgery connects athletes with hernia specialists who have experience in sports hernia repair.\n\n\n\nCall MySurgery at 8588967050 or WhatsApp us for a free consultation with an experienced hernia surgeon in your city. Callback within 30 minutes.\n\nBook Free Consultation: mysurgery.in/contact | WhatsApp: wa.me/918588967050",
