    body: "Spine surgery in India costs Rs 2,40,000 to Rs 9,60,000 depending on the procedure and hospital. Health insurance can cover most of this cost.\n\nIs Spine Surgery Covered by Health Insurance in India?\n\nYes. Spine surgery is covered by all major health insurance policies in India under inpatient hospitalisation. This includes lumbar disc surgery (microdiscectomy, TLIF, PLIF), cervical disc surgery, laminectomy, spinal fusion, minimally invasive spine surgery, and deformity correction.\n\nWaiting Period for Spine Surgery Insurance\n\nIf you have a history of back pain, disc disease, or spinal stenosis before taking the policy, these may be classified as pre-existing conditions. Most insurers apply a 2-year waiting period. If the condition is acute and new, it is covered immediately. PIVD (Prolapsed Intervertebral Disc) is specifically listed as a common pre-existing condition in many policy exclusion lists — check carefully.\n\nWhat Is Covered?\n\nSurgeon fees and anaesthesia. OT and ICU charges. Hospital stay — typically 3 to 7 days for minimally invasive and 7 to 14 days for open fusion. Implants: pedicle screws, cages, and other spinal implants are covered but often with a sub-limit. Check your policy for implant sub-limit. Physiotherapy during hospitalisation. Pre-hospitalisation: investigations like MRI, CT, nerve conduction studies (30 days). Post-hospitalisation: physiotherapy, medications, follow-up MRI (60 to 90 days).\n\nImplant Sub-Limit Warning\n\nSpine surgeries often require expensive implants (Rs 80,000 to Rs 3,00,000). Many policies have implant sub-limits of Rs 50,000 to Rs 1,50,000. If your implant cost exceeds the sub-limit you pay the difference out of pocket. MySurgery insurance team checks implant coverage before surgery and selects hospitals that use implants within your policy's sub-limit where possible.\n\nMinimally Invasive vs Open Spine Surgery — Insurance Coverage\n\nBoth are covered equally by insurance. However, minimally invasive spine surgery typically has a shorter hospital stay which can reduce the overall claim amount but also reduce your out-of-pocket proportional expenses.\n\nHow to Claim Cashless Insurance for Spine Surgery\n\nInform your insurer 3 to 5 days before planned surgery. Submit MRI reports, surgeon's advice for surgery, and estimate from the hospital. Pre-auth approval typically within 4 to 8 hours. MySurgery manages this entire process at no charge.\n\nCall MySurgery at 8588967050 for a free insurance check for spine surgery within 30 minutes.",
