    body: "Hip replacement surgery in India costs Rs 1,80,000 to Rs 3,60,000. Health insurance covers most of this if you understand the key terms.\n\nIs Hip Replacement Covered by Health Insurance in India?\n\nYes. Total hip replacement (THR) and partial hip replacement (hemiarthroplasty) are covered by all major health insurance policies in India. Coverage is under inpatient hospitalisation.\n\nWaiting Period for Hip Replacement Insurance\n\nHip arthritis and avascular necrosis (AVN) are common pre-existing conditions that trigger waiting periods. Most insurers apply a 2 to 4 year waiting period for joint replacement if arthritis was diagnosed before the policy was taken. Fracture of the hip neck requiring emergency replacement may be covered immediately as an acute event.\n\nKey Policies: Star Health — 2 years. HDFC Ergo — 3 years. Care Health — 2 years. Bajaj Allianz — 2 years. ICICI Lombard — 4 years.\n\nWhat Is Covered?\n\nSurgeon fee, anaesthesia, and OT charges. Hospital stay of 5 to 7 days. Hip implant: femoral stem, acetabular cup, femoral head, and liner. Major brands include Zimmer Biomet, Stryker, and DePuy. Physiotherapy during hospitalisation. Pre-hospitalisation: X-rays, MRI, blood tests (30 days). Post-hospitalisation: physiotherapy and medications (60 to 90 days).\n\nImplant Sub-Limit — The Most Important Item to Check\n\nHip implants cost Rs 60,000 to Rs 2,50,000 depending on the brand and type. Many policies have implant sub-limits of Rs 50,000 to Rs 1,00,000. If the implant exceeds your sub-limit you pay the difference. MySurgery works with hospitals that offer quality implants at sub-limit-friendly price points when possible, and advises on implant choice before surgery to minimise out-of-pocket costs.\n\nRoom Rent Sub-Limit\n\nAs with all surgeries, choose a hospital room within your entitled category (1% of sum insured per day) to avoid proportional reduction of the entire claim.\n\nHow to Claim Cashless Insurance for Hip Replacement\n\nInform your insurer 3 to 5 days before surgery. Submit X-rays, surgeon's advice, and hospital estimate. MySurgery coordinates the full pre-auth process. Approval in 4 to 8 hours for planned procedures.\n\nCall MySurgery at 8588967050 for a free insurance check and hip replacement cost estimate within 30 minutes.",
