    keywords: ["bariatric surgery insurance india 2026", "weight loss surgery covered health insurance india", "bariatric surgery cashless claim india"],
    body: "Bariatric surgery in India costs Rs 3,00,000 to Rs 6,00,000. Insurance coverage has improved significantly after IRDAI's 2024 mandate. Here is what you need to know.\n\nIs Bariatric Surgery Covered by Health Insurance in India?\n\nYes — but with conditions. IRDAI (Insurance Regulatory and Development Authority of India) mandated in April 2024 that all comprehensive health insurance policies must cover bariatric surgery if medically necessary. This was a landmark change. Before 2024, most policies excluded bariatric surgery. Policies issued or renewed after April 2024 must include coverage if your BMI and health conditions meet the medical necessity criteria.\n\nEligibility Criteria for Bariatric Surgery Insurance Coverage\n\nBMI of 40 kg/m2 or above, regardless of other conditions. BMI of 35 to 39.9 with at least one serious obesity-related comorbidity: Type 2 diabetes, hypertension, obstructive sleep apnea, heart disease, non-alcoholic fatty liver disease, or severe joint disease. The decision for surgery must be made by a qualified bariatric surgeon with documentation of failed conservative treatment (diet, exercise, medication) for at least 6 months.\n\nWaiting Period for Bariatric Surgery Insurance\n\nMost policies impose a 2 to 3 year waiting period for bariatric surgery as it is classified as a planned surgery for a chronic condition (obesity). Check your policy issuance date and waiting period. If your policy was issued more than 3 years ago, bariatric surgery may be covered now.\n\nWhat Is Covered?\n\nSleeve gastrectomy, gastric bypass, and mini-gastric bypass surgery. Anaesthesia, OT, and ICU charges. Hospital stay of 3 to 5 days. Pre-operative evaluation: nutritionist assessment, psychiatric evaluation, pre-anaesthesia workup. Post-operative stay and immediate follow-up.\n\nWhat Is Not Covered?\n\nLong-term nutritional supplements and vitamins after discharge. Psychological counselling beyond hospitalisation. Revision bariatric surgery in many policies.\n\nHow to Get Insurance Approval for Bariatric Surgery\n\nThe insurer will require detailed documentation. BMI documentation with height and weight. Records of conservative treatment failure for 6 months. Comorbidity documentation — HbA1c for diabetes, BP records for hypertension. Bariatric surgeon's recommendation letter. Nutritionist and psychiatrist clearance letters. MySurgery works with a team of bariatric surgeons at NABH-accredited hospitals and helps compile the complete documentation package for insurance approval.\n\nCall MySurgery at 8588967050 for a free bariatric surgery insurance eligibility check within 30 minutes.",
