    keywords: ["liver transplant insurance india 2026", "liver transplant covered health insurance india", "liver transplant cashless claim india"],
    body: "Liver transplant is among the most expensive procedures in India costing Rs 24,00,000 to Rs 42,00,000. Here is everything you need to know about insurance coverage.\n\nIs Liver Transplant Covered by Health Insurance in India?\n\nYes. Liver transplant is covered under inpatient hospitalisation by comprehensive health insurance policies with an adequate sum insured. Most standard policies with Rs 5 to 10 lakh sum insured will not cover the full cost. A sum insured of Rs 25 lakh or higher is recommended. Super top-up policies can supplement your base coverage cost-effectively.\n\nWaiting Period for Liver Transplant Insurance\n\nLiver disease (cirrhosis, hepatitis, NASH) is typically a pre-existing condition by the time transplant is needed. If declared at policy inception, a 2 to 4 year waiting period applies. Acute liver failure events may be covered immediately if there is no prior diagnosis of liver disease. Check your policy exclusion list specifically for organ transplants — a few policies still exclude all organ transplants.\n\nPolicies That Cover Liver Transplant: Star Health Senior Citizen Red Carpet (for older patients), HDFC Ergo Optima Secure, Care Supreme, Bajaj Allianz Health Guard Gold, Niva Bupa ReAssure 2.0.\n\nWhat Is Covered?\n\nRecipient surgery: ICU stay of 7 to 14 days, ward stay, surgery, anaesthesia, OT charges, medications during hospitalisation. Living donor evaluation: Blood group compatibility tests, liver imaging, fitness evaluation for the donor. Living donor surgery: Most comprehensive policies cover the donor's surgical hospitalisation separately. Immunosuppressants during hospitalisation: Tacrolimus, mycophenolate, and steroids during hospital stay. Pre and post-hospitalisation: Typically 30 to 60 days pre and 60 to 90 days post.\n\nWhat Is Typically Not Covered?\n\nLifelong immunosuppressant medications post-discharge. Deceased donor (cadaveric) transplant organ procurement charges in some policies. Rejection episodes beyond a defined number in some policies. Post-transplant outpatient monitoring.\n\nRecommended Sum Insured and Top-Up Strategy\n\nBase policy: Rs 10 to 15 lakh. Super top-up: Rs 20 to 25 lakh with a deductible equal to your base sum insured. This combination provides Rs 30 to 40 lakh of effective coverage at a fraction of buying a single Rs 35 lakh policy. MySurgery insurance advisors can help structure the right combination for your family.\n\nHow to Claim Cashless Insurance for Liver Transplant\n\nLiver transplant requires advance planning with the insurer. Inform the insurer at least 7 to 10 days before planned transplant. Submit transplant team assessment, donor compatibility report, and MELD score documentation. MySurgery coordinates between the transplant programme, insurance desk, and insurer for seamless cashless processing.\n\nCall MySurgery at 8588967050 for a free insurance coverage check and liver transplant cost estimation within 24 hours.",
