    body: "Getting an Indian Medical Visa is straightforward when you have the right documents. Here is everything African patients need to know.\n\nWhat Is Indian Medical Visa?\n\nIndia has a dedicated Medical Visa (MV) category specifically for patients travelling to India for medical treatment. It is different from a tourist visa and is specifically for hospital-based treatment. You can also bring up to 2 accompanying family members on Medical Attendant Visa (MX).\n\nDocuments Required for Indian Medical Visa\n\nValid passport with at least 6 months validity and 2 blank pages. Recent passport-size photograph (white background). Completed Indian visa application form (apply online at indianvisaonline.gov.in). Hospital invitation letter from a recognised Indian hospital. MySurgery provides this free of charge within 48 hours. Your latest medical reports and doctor's recommendation for treatment in India. Proof of financial means — bank statement showing sufficient funds for treatment and stay. Return flight booking or confirmed itinerary. Accommodation proof — hotel booking or hospital accommodation confirmation.\n\nWhere to Apply by Country\n\nNigeria: Indian High Commission Lagos (VFS Global), Indian High Commission Abuja. Kenya: Indian High Commission Nairobi. Ethiopia: Indian Embassy Addis Ababa. Ghana: Indian High Commission Accra. Tanzania: Indian High Commission Dar es Salaam. Uganda: Indian High Commission Kampala. For countries without Indian representation, applications go to the nearest Indian mission.\n\nVisa Fee and Processing Time\n\nVisa fee: Varies by country, typically $50 to $80 USD equivalent. Processing time: 3 to 7 business days in most African countries. For urgent medical situations, request expedited processing — the embassy can sometimes process within 48 hours with a supporting letter from the hospital.\n\nMedical Attendant Visa (MX) for Family\n\nYou can bring up to 2 family members as medical attendants. Each attendant applies separately with their passport, photograph, application form, and a copy of the patient's Medical Visa application and hospital invitation letter. Same documents, same process, same timeline.\n\nValidity of Indian Medical Visa\n\nMedical Visa is typically granted for the duration of treatment plus 6 months, or up to 1 year, with triple entry. This allows the patient to return for follow-up without reapplying. Extensions are possible in India at the Foreigners Regional Registration Office (FRRO) if treatment requires a longer stay.\n\nHow MySurgery Helps with Visa\n\nMySurgery provides: hospital invitation letter within 48 hours, a comprehensive treatment plan document supporting your visa application, guidance on completing the online application form, and a 24/7 WhatsApp helpline for visa queries. We have helped over 5,000 African patients successfully obtain Indian Medical Visas.\n\nWhatsApp MySurgery on +91 8588967050 to get your hospital invitation letter within 48 hours and start your visa process today.",
